[phaedrus@milton.acs.washington.edu (The Wanderer) writes:]
[] I did come across a few bugs that I didn't see previously mentioned,
[] 1) When you dip a scroll into a potion to get a scroll of blank paper, it
[] becomes an unidentified scroll if you haven't found a scroll of blank paper

That's a bug/feature of the game itself. Simply reading the (already known!)
scroll takes care of that problem and you won't lose the scroll, either.

[] 2) Mimics are 100% identifiable.  (This may be a feature. :) )  If you use
[] the / command and identify the space with the mimic, it says "I've never
[] heard of such items" rather than identifying whatever shape the mimic is...

The mimics shape, "]", in this case is unknown. I've always thought that the
game should identify this as "Shhhh, no one talks about this anymore ...".
I can't recall how it handles mimics really imitating objects, I thought
that worked. In any event, mimics are easy for other reasons as well ...

[] 3) "Just show scores" doesn't work; it returns to the Finder immediately.

Actually, it returns to the Finder after briefly flashing the message
"Can't find any entries for you", even if you do have entries. I'll bet
the MacDev Team has this fixed even as you're reading this note ...

